{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfxe91ns","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"physics","chapter":"magnetism","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"moving-coil-galvanometer","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1--the-sensitivity-of-a-moving-coil-galvanomet-jee-advanced-physics-motion-njty7mpydfqefoya","content":"<p>STATEMENT 1 : The sensitivity of a moving coil galvanometer is increased by placing a suitable magnetic material as a core inside the coil.</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p>STATEMENT 2 : Soft iron has a high magnetic permeability and cannot be easily magnetized or demagnetized.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a NOT CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>Statement 1 is true.</p>\n<p>We know that,</p>\n<p>Sensitivity <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.816ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.038ex\" height=\"2.853ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -900.3 5320.7 1260.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1055.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(232.4,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><rect width=\"556.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2129.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(3185.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1647,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(798.8,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><rect width=\"1894.9\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>If we place soft iron in magnetic field it get magnetise so magnetic field increases. Hence, sensitivity of a moving coil will also increase.</p>\n<p>Therefore, <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.355ex\" height=\"3.19ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1410 1041 1410\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mover\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(120.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(41,799)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.802ex\" height=\"2.8ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -892.5 796.4 1237.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(232.4,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D703\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D703\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D43C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43C\"></use></g><rect width=\"556.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> also increases.</p>\n<p>When we place any suitable magnetic material inside the core, the magnetic field will increase.</p>\n<p>Statement 2 is wrong because soft iron can be easily magnetized and de magnetized.</p>"}]}